{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1175148-astral-projection-via-dreams","id":1175148,"title":"Astral Projection via Dreams","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-11T06:26:33-08:00","id":1175148,"title":"Astral Projection via Dreams","content":"What are the thoughts on using Mind 3 to enter dreams and the Dream Realm and then employing Spirit 3 from there to basically Astral travel? <br /> <br /> Is this plausible or do you think it's a no go without Mind 4 to form the astral cord / link?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T07:47:05-08:00","id":1175170,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure you can't leave the Dreamlands mentally until you hit Mind 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T11:01:55-08:00","id":1175226,"title":"","content":"Simply employing Spirit 3 wouldn't be enough. As a Storyteller I'd rule that the character would have to find a place, where the Dreaming connects to the Umbra. It is logically possible, but that doesn't mean it should be always accessible. If someone want's to lower/change sphere requirements for his magical tricks and has a good explanation for it, he should work for this. A medium quest through the Dreaming (maybe a single session) should be the minimum in my eyes, in this situation.<br /> Otherwise the players start dancing all over the rules with weird ideas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T06:34:32-08:00","id":1175438,"title":"","content":"Not trying to dance on the rules. He'll, I'm the ST. Was just wondering if people thought Spirit could breakthrough the barrier of the Dreamscape if one's psyche was already there.<br /> <br /> I guess if you think about it it's would be kinda weird for psychic energy to become epherma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T08:22:46-08:00","id":1175468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1175148-astral-projection-via-dreams?p=1175438#post1175438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not trying to dance on the rules. He'll, I'm the ST. Was just wondering if people thought Spirit could breakthrough the barrier of the Dreamscape if one's psyche was already there.<br /> <br /> I guess if you think about it it's would be kinda weird for psychic energy to become epherma.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not if it's in the higher umbra. At least in my headcannon, there would be a number of connections, where a smart mage or a especially gifted dream creature (read: Fey with much specialized knowledge) could break (or even stumble) through. Hell, maybe you'd find a way, where the connection is actually fluid. There's a way, that connects the Malfeas with the Dreaming, so why not some different, much more logical paths?<br /> I also didn't want to imply you were trying to dance the rules. Quite the opposite, actually. I just wanted to point out that this could be actually possible if you, as the ST, are okay with it and the players put enough effort in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T13:32:58-08:00","id":1176375,"title":"","content":"Using dream travel as a <i>technique </i>or as an integral part of a character's paradigm is certainly legit. However, using Mind:3 to project to the dream(s) of another isn't sufficient for Spirit:3 to take you &quot;higher&quot; -- you still need either Mind:4 or 5 (depending on duration/attention, etc.) to do that, generally speaking. (It's that editions-long difference between conceptual technique -- applied (P)aradigm -- and game mechanics: it can be a part of your character's paradigm that he has to project mentally into dreams *first* and *then* move &quot;upwards&quot; to the High/Astral Umbra, but regardless the mechanics would require Mind:4+.<br /> <br /> Still, though -- I get where the OP is coming from. In a Pillar-based or Alt/Minor-Sphere based variation, such a combination concept would/could be easily applied (and even expected for some characters)... but if trying to keep with the general metaphysics of Mage, the Spirit:3 add-on isn't sufficient. (Like you said, though -- you're the St, so tweak it as you will...).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}